  "validation_notes": [
    "SaveRestoreRegression, FixedWingSaveRegression and AirSaveContinuityRegression require fixed simulation stepping for their frame-count-based waits. They pass with --fixed-fps 60; unthrottled failures are not model-save failures.",
    "Animation failures reproduced by the audit came from interpolated camera teleports and assuming rendered frames were simulation ticks. The corrected fixture verifies settled wreck poses without changing production infantry motion.",
    "Native LOD regression counts isolated rendered primitives, not frame time. Compatibility does not support the native pose path and keeps the ordinary imported LODs.",
    "All modified/new GDScripts pass gdformat --check and gdlint; Python generators parse; git diff --check passes."
  ],
  "audit_decisions": [
    "Keep the existing smooth -30 degree camera and opaque scenery; visibility-owned silhouettes passed real building/mountain/cliff occlusion checks without changing navigation footprints.",
    "Use generated index-only mesh LODs to retain articulated poses. Imported GLBs already had LODs; the native batch merge was dropping them.",
    "Reduce Frontier wheel primitives from four material surfaces to three. Preserve metal/rubber finishes, team materials and baked weathering; no whole-roster atlas rewrite.",
    "Keep already-readable low-poly walkers; triangle-count differences alone are not a visual defect."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The broad Skirmish fixture has pre-existing unsupported-faction model requests and cleanup failures. The first error was reproduced on the unchanged baseline.",
    "Compatibility reports pre-existing BPTC-to-RGBA8 texture conversion warnings. Occlusion and scenery are checked on a neutral floor in both renderers; full-map Compatibility rendering is not certified.",
    "No frame-time performance claim: topology and rendered primitive reductions are measured, but no representative 70-100-unit benchmark was run."
  ],
